    "master_and_main_rationale": "ajoe734/pantheon master and ajoe734/execute-plans main remain unchanged and do not require 'Pantheon canonical review gate' because promote pull requests do not run the gate workflow.",
    "direct_delivery_rule": "Operator-directed direct deliveries require a task/<TASK-ID> branch with an operator acceptance proof tag (refs/tags/pantheon-review/operator-accept/<head_sha> via operator-accept, or a mechanical delivery:tooling PR for eligible tooling-only changes) because GitHub now rejects a merge into either dev branch without a green 'Pantheon canonical review gate'.",
    "residual_risk": "GitHub now refuses a merge into either dev branch (pantheon dev or execute-plans dev) without a green 'Pantheon canonical review gate' status posted by the GitHub Actions workflow (app_id 15368, github-actions[bot]). However, a holder of the shared ajoe734 GitHub credential can still deliberately push a refs/tags/pantheon-review/* proof tag or add the delivery:tooling label directly on GitHub; only a separate review identity (review_gate.github_review_identity='independent') closes that.",
    "rollback_order": [
      "1. Remove 'Pantheon canonical review gate' from GitHub branch protection required_status_checks in both repositories (ajoe734/pantheon dev and ajoe734/execute-plans dev).",
      "2. Set review_gate.github_review_bridge_required to false and remove 'Pantheon canonical review gate' from branch_workflow.task_pr.required_status_checks in .orchestrator/config.json, then promote the runtime (the verifier scripts/git/canonical_review_gate_ci.py stops publishing once the flag is false, so removing the branch-protection check first prevents blocking every merge into dev)."
    ]
  },
